-- Ontology (Ch.18) — capability-name concepts, reworked (CR-086 step one).
-- Owner, 2026-08-18: "Capability packs are essentially process fragments done
-- by a team... The platform uses code to identify the process fragment. The
-- tenants may use the same process, but call it by a different name."
--
-- This migration replaces the original 23-row seed outright with the
-- vocabulary from Book 3 Ch.10's "Capability" table (design/foundations/03_
-- Book 3 (Refined)/02_Part 2/Chapter 10.md) — a full generational rewrite of
-- the concept_type, not an amendment to it. CR-086 confirmed there are still
-- zero consumers of capability-name concepts anywhere in the codebase (the
-- functional `capabilities` table — one row per Pack contributing a
-- capability — is a separate, unrelated structure; see CR-085), so this
-- replace has zero blast radius on running code.
--
-- Naming discipline unchanged from the original migration (owner: "simple
-- rules. small case no spaces"): code is lowercase-hyphenated, default_label
-- carries the exact human wording. DELETE-then-INSERT (rather than the
-- original's rename-in-place UPDATE) makes this migration naturally
-- idempotent across replays — no defensive guards needed against a
-- resurrected stale row, unlike the original's CR-059 workaround.

